{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>upon Mount Zion, which is desolate</b> – past tense verb, like כאשר אהב (Genesis 27:14):" "<b>foxes</b> – their habit is to be in ruins:" "<b>walked on it</b> – the walkers, like ויחנטו אותו (Genesis 50:26). And הלכו is in the sense of walking from the heavy conjugation, and it is an intransitive verb. And because I found עָרוֹם הִלְּכוּ (Job 24:10), I needed the first grammatical analysis:"], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:15.484041127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}